# Generated by `pnpm codegen` (buf + protoc-gen-es) into the workspace package,
# so pnpm can resolve `workspace:*` against something that exists on disk.
#
# NOT committed, deliberately. Bazel is the authority for what ships — the
# published tarball is assembled by //schemas/proto:proto_ts_pkg — so a checked-in
# copy here would be a second producer of the same types with no gate keeping them
# equal. That is exactly the failure meridian-k8s hit with its vendored proto tree:
# taken at schemas 0.17.0, silently drifted, lost Slot.sub_view, and nothing
# noticed because nothing compared them.
#
# The cost is that a fresh clone must run `pnpm install` (which runs codegen via
# `prepare`) before typechecking. That is one command, needs no protoc, no Bazel,
# no registry and no credentials, and it is the price of having exactly one
# committed source of truth.
packages/proto-ts/proto/
packages/proto-ts/google/
